---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { GLOSSARY } from '../data/glossary';

const ld = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'DefinedTermSet',
  name: 'Nylon 3D Printing Glossary',
  hasDefinedTerm: GLOSSARY.map((t) => ({
    '@type': 'DefinedTerm',
    name: t.term,
    description: t.definition,
    url: `https://nylon3dp.com/glossary/#${t.id}`,
  })),
};
---

<Base
  title="Nylon 3D Printing Glossary | Nylon3DP"
  description="Short definitions for nylon 3D printing: PA11, PA12, PA6, SLS, MJF, SAF, refresh ratio, glass- and carbon-filled nylon, annealing, vapor smoothing and HDT."
  jsonLd={ld}
>
  <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Glossary</p>
  <h1>Nylon 3D printing glossary</h1>
  <div class="quick-answer">
    <p class="qa-label">Quick answer</p>
    <p>The essential vocabulary of nylon 3D printing in one place: the polyamide grades (PA11, PA12, PA6), the processes (SLS, MJF, SAF, FDM), and the concepts — refresh ratio, filled grades, moisture, post-processing — that decide whether a nylon part succeeds.</p>
  </div>

  <p>{GLOSSARY.map((t, i) => (<>{i > 0 && ' · '}<a href={`#${t.id}`}>{t.term.split(' (')[0]}</a></>))}</p>

  <dl class="glossary">
    {GLOSSARY.map((t) => (
      <>
        <dt id={t.id}>{t.term}</dt>
        <dd>{t.definition}</dd>
      </>
    ))}
  </dl>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: November 2026. Definitions are kept consistent with the material and process pages that cite them.</p>
</Base>
